    "probe": "ransom-note-b",
    "of": "examples/probes/ransom-note-b.json",
    "target": "same target as ransom-note, different object: one word stacked down a whole page on cut strips, rather than a slogan hand-set across the middle",
    "method": "the same five rows at the same five transforms. Each strip is now a rect clip over five overlapping torn `object.bowl` fragments, so the ends are scissor cuts and the long edges are a seeded tear -- there is no fragment in the pack anywhere near 5:1 and `span` scales uniformly, so a page-width torn strip has to be assembled out of square ones. Five real faces across four roles replace two Regulars. This is the probe that takes the screen: `halftone` at cell 4, angle 15, which is the row `ransom-note` could not afford.",
    "notDone": "the screen is whole-canvas and two-tone, so the three stocks survive as three dot densities rather than three colours and the multiply overprint is flattened to a dark patch. The colour evidence for both is in `ransom-note`, which keeps its ink and stays faked on the screen. `transform.rotate` still quantises to a whole degree."
  },
